08:13.880 --> 08:17.290
Just be sure to stay real close.

08:17.540 --> 08:18.380
We will!

08:18.750 --> 08:23.880
I'm Keitaro Gentoga. This is Eiko Hozuki.

08:24.130 --> 08:25.460
Nice to meet you!

08:25.880 --> 08:28.960
And this here is Yayoi-chan, her cousin.

08:32.380 --> 08:34.790
Shami-san, did you come here for an exorcism?

08:35.380 --> 08:37.290
Yeah, you could say that.

08:38.130 --> 08:44.460
Then for safety's sake, let me share with you
the story of what makes this place haunted.

08:45.330 --> 08:46.170
Let's hear it.

08:46.920 --> 08:48.420
Here's what I've got.

08:49.420 --> 08:53.130
The Old I Watergate,
known locally as the "Red Watergate."

08:54.130 --> 09:02.790
After a 1924 flood ravaged the area,
they built gates to control the flow of riverwater.

09:03.750 --> 09:07.580
Though a newly-built facility has rended this one defunct,

09:07.790 --> 09:12.830
the old watergate has been kept preserved
as a registered historic landmark.

09:13.630 --> 09:17.920
During the day, people use the area
around the watergate for recreation,

09:18.380 --> 09:22.790
but when night falls, the ghosts come out,
or so say the many who've seen them here.

09:23.460 --> 09:28.250
People have claimed it was haunted
since as early as the 1960s.

09:29.290 --> 09:31.790
Here's what some people have seen:

09:32.540 --> 09:36.830
Ghosts lying in the same place
where their bodies were found.

09:37.960 --> 09:40.830
Dark, humanoid shadows on the water.

09:41.630 --> 09:45.420
Dismembered limbs floating on the surface.

09:46.330 --> 09:49.460
A female spirit, standing atop the watergate.

09:50.460 --> 09:54.750
An increased rate of suicide by hanging
in the years since the watergate was built.

09:55.710 --> 09:59.500
A jizo statue erected to memorialize
those who drowned was found beheaded.

10:00.250 --> 10:02.170
And that's where this list ends.

10:02.790 --> 10:06.750
Yayoi-chan, I've been wondering...

10:07.380 --> 10:12.960
